 "tips": {
  "sub": "PunchPaw is a punch compressor for drums and bass: kick, snare, drum bus and parallel crush. It is not a mastering tool. It is fast, hard-knee and adds colour, so for a whole song use a gentle bus or mastering compressor instead.",
  "cheek": "Double-click the wood to reset the window to 100%.",
  "dial": "Analogue-style level meter. Choose what it shows with the Show buttons: input level, output level, or how much the unit turns the sound down. The colour band marks safe (blue), warning (purple) and clip (pink).",
  "curve": "Level in (across) against level out (up), both in dB. The curve follows Threshold, Ratio, Knee, Output and Ceiling. The white dot is the live signal.",
  "shape": "The loudness shape of each hit in dB. Grey is what goes in, the coloured fill is what comes out, pink bars from the top show how much was turned down. Watch the front of the kick to see the punch.",
  "hist": "How much the unit turned the signal down, in dB, over the last six seconds.",
  "cvIn": "Input peak level in dB. Blue is safe, purple is the warning zone, pink is clipping. The top cap stays pink after a clip; click to clear it.",
  "cvOut": "Output peak level in dB, after Output, Mix and Ceiling. The top cap stays pink after a clip; click to clear it.",
  "pkIn": "Highest recent input peak, in dB.",
  "pkOut": "Highest recent output peak, in dB.",
  "pPrev": "Previous preset.",
  "pName": "Open the preset browser. Double-click to rename your own presets.",
  "pNext": "Next preset.",
  "pSave": "Save these settings as your own preset. Asks before overwriting.",
  "bBypass": "Bypass: hear the dry signal to compare with the processed sound (B). The meters keep moving.",
  "bGuide": "Short guide and keyboard shortcuts.",
  "bSettings": "Info bubbles, power saving, colour look.",
  "bAbout": "About PunchPaw, support and where your files live."
 },
